{"orgCode":"9100","name":"Tax Relief","agencyCode":"8000","agencyName":"General Government","description":"This budget provides funding for cities and counties to help defray the loss of revenue as a result of the Homeowners' Property Tax Relief Program, a program that provides California homeowners assistance through a $7,000 exemption from property tax, and the Open Space Subventions Program, a program that provides tax relief to individuals who agreed to hold their land as open space under the Williamson Act of 1965. This budget also receives loan repayments from people participating in the Senior Citizens and Disabled Citizens Property Tax Postponement Program.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":384449,"cy":420001,"by":410001},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0}},"programs":{"id":"exp/8000/9100","kind":"department","name":"Tax Relief","code":"9100","amounts":{"py":384449,"cy":420001,"by":410001},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001},"special":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/7500","kind":"program","name":"Homeowners' Property Tax Relief","code":"7500","amounts":{"py":384448,"cy":420000,"by":410000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385144,"cy":413000,"by":403000},"special":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"7500 - HOMEOWNERS' PROPERTY TAX RELIEF\n\nIn order to reduce California taxpayers' property tax burden, the California Constitution exempts homeowners from paying property taxes on the first $7,000 of the assessed value of their principal place of residence. The Constitution requires the state to reimburse local governments for revenues lost due to the homeowners' exemption. This Program also receives repayments from persons participating in the Senior Citizens and Disabled Citizens Property Tax Postponement Program, whereby the state makes property tax payments for qualified homeowners in exchange for the participants making repayment when they relinquish ownership.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":384448,"cy":420000,"by":410000}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/7500/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":385144,"cy":413000,"by":403000},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385144,"cy":413000,"by":403000}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":385144,"cy":413000,"by":403000}}}},{"id":"exp/8000/9100/7500/f3268","kind":"fund","name":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Citizens Property Tax Postponement Fund","code":"3268","amounts":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000}}}}]},{"id":"exp/8000/9100/7505","kind":"program","name":"Subventions for Open Space","code":"7505","amounts":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"description":"7505 - SUBVENTIONS FOR OPEN SPACE\n\nThe Williamson Act permits cities and counties to enter into contracts with landowners to limit the use of land to agricultural, scenic, and open space purposes. Article XIII, section 8, of the California Constitution permits land under such restrictions to be assessed at other than market value based on its limited uses. The state provides reimbursements to cities and counties to partially defray the loss of property tax revenues. The Department of Conservation administers this program.","extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/7505/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":1,"cy":1,"by":1}}}}]}],"sources":[{"label":"ebudget.ca.gov API: orgProgram/9100","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/api/budget/e/2026-27/orgProgram/9100"},{"label":"Detailed Expenditures by Program (PDF)","url":"https://ebudget.ca.gov/2026-27/pdf/Enacted/GovernorsBudget/8000/9100.pdf"}],"extra":{"legalCitations":"PROGRAM AUTHORITY\n\n7500-Homeowners' Property Tax Relief:\nCalifornia Constitution, Article XIII, sections 3 and 25; Government Code sections 16100-16101.5, 16120-16122, and 16180.\nRevenue and Taxation Code sections 20501-20646.\n\n7505-Subventions for Open Space:\nCalifornia Constitution, Article XIII, section 8; Government Code sections 51244, 51244.3, 16100-16101.5 and 16140-16154; Revenue and Taxation Code sections 421-430.5."}},"funding":{"id":"exp/8000/9100/funding","kind":"root","name":"Tax Relief: Funding by fund and appropriation","amounts":{"py":384449,"cy":420001,"by":410001},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001},"special":{"py":-696,"cy":7000,"by":7000}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/funding/general","kind":"fundType","name":"General Fund","code":"general","amounts":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/fund/0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","fundClass":"G","support":{"py":385145,"cy":413001,"by":403001},"capitalOutlay":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0}},"children":[{"id":"exp/8000/9100/fund/0001/9100-101-0001","kind":"item","name":"101 Budget Act appropriation","amounts":{"py":377645,"cy":410001,"by":400001},"extra":{"lineType":"item","appropriationType":"Local Assistance"},"code":"9100-101-0001"},{"id":"exp/8000/9100/fund/0001/9100-111-0001","kind":"item","name":"111 Budget Act appropriation (transfer to Senior Citizens and Disabled Citizens Property Tax Postponement Fund)","amounts":{"py":7500,"cy":3000,"by":3000},"extra":{"lineType":"item","appropriat